{"tool_name":"rapmap","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","debian","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"rapmap","identifiers":["biotools:rapmap","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw277"],"license":"GPL-3.0+","summary":"Rapid sensitive and accurate dna read mapping via quasi-mapping","home_url":"https://github.com/COMBINE-lab/RapMap","keywords":["RNA","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Transcriptome","Transcriptomics","Sequence analysis"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4796},"biotools":{"id":"rapmap","home":"https://github.com/COMBINE-lab/RapMap","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"RapMap is a tool implementing quasi-mapping and is capable of mapping sequencing reads to a target transcriptome substantially faster than existing alignment tools.","addition_date":"2018-10-06T11:37:02Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T16:54:08Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rapmap","credit":[{"email":"asrivastava@cs.stonybrook.edu","name":"Avi Srivastava","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9798-2079","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"rob.patro@cs.stonybrook.edu","name":"Rob Patro","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/COMBINE-lab/RapMap/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2520"}]}],"name":"RapMap","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw277","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author 2016. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: The alignment of sequencing reads to a transcriptome is a common and important step in many RNA-seq analysis tasks. When aligning RNA-seq reads directly to a transcriptome (as is common in the de novo setting or when a trusted reference annotation is available), care must be taken to report the potentially large number of multi-mapping locations per read. This can pose a substantial computational burden for existing aligners, and can considerably slow downstream analysis. Results: We introduce a novel concept, quasi-mapping, and an efficient algorithm implementing this approach for mapping sequencing reads to a transcriptome. By attempting only to report the potential loci of origin of a sequencing read, and not the base-to-base alignment by which it derives from the reference, RapMap - our tool implementing quasi-mapping - is capable of mapping sequencing reads to a target transcriptome substantially faster than existing alignment tools. The algorithm we use to implement quasi-mapping uses several efficient data structures and takes advantage of the special structure of shared sequence prevalent in transcriptomes to rapidly provide highly-accurate mapping information. We demonstrate how quasi-mapping can be successfully applied to the problems of transcript-level quantification from RNA-seq reads and the clustering of contigs from de novo assembled transcriptomes into biologically meaningful groups.","authors":[{"name":"Gupta N."},{"name":"Patro R."},{"name":"Sarkar H."},{"name":"Srivastava A."}],"citationCount":49,"date":"2016-06-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"RapMap: A rapid, sensitive and accurate tool for mapping RNA-seq reads to transcriptomes"},"pmcid":"PMC4908361","pmid":"27307617","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RapMap","home":"https://bio.tools/rapmap","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"RapMap is a tool implementing quasi-mapping and is capable of mapping sequencing reads to a target transcriptome substantially faster than existing alignment tools.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebe